So for Bitcoin staking, the only thing you have is duration risk or liquidity risk.

410
00:30:15.400 --> 00:30:26.580
And what I mean by that is if you're locking up those funds for, you know, at least a day, I believe, is the minimum time, you can't go set in that or trade in or something, right?

411
00:30:26.680 --> 00:30:28.860
So, like, there's only, like, liquidity from that point of view.

412
00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:34.340
The vast majority of folks that are doing Bitcoin staking do not have that in mind on, like, a one-day time horizon.

413
00:30:34.340 --> 00:30:40.800
But it is important just to note that you cannot do both because you're actually locking up those funds on Bitcoin itself.

414
00:30:41.220 --> 00:30:49.640
When it comes to, you know, the full Bitcoin DeFi aspects of Core, that's a little bit of a different ballgame in that you're in a full EVM ecosystem, right?

