00:37:25.880 --> 00:37:28.080
Then you have, I'm just willing to go stake my Bitcoin.

510
00:37:28.260 --> 00:37:29.400
That's the next biggest bucket.

511
00:37:30.060 --> 00:37:34.400
Dual staking is that middle ground because it says, hey, I'm willing to go stake my Bitcoin.

512
00:37:34.400 --> 00:37:41.420
And I'm willing to take some principal risk in the form of the Core token in order to get higher rates of return on my Bitcoin.

513
00:37:41.980 --> 00:37:44.800
And Core and Bitcoin are correlated like 0.95 or something.

514
00:37:45.040 --> 00:37:47.220
So there's principal risk that's directly aligned with Bitcoin.

515
00:37:47.560 --> 00:37:49.320
You know, you would do that with what you will.

516
00:37:49.820 --> 00:37:54.320
And then the final step of that is Bitcoin DeFi, where you wrap or you bridge or you come over.

517
00:37:54.420 --> 00:37:55.940
And that's the smallest segment today.

518
00:37:56.420 --> 00:38:03.200
So this is really meant to help bring people along that spectrum and allow them to earn DeFi yields, if you will,

519
00:38:03.200 --> 00:38:07.020
or DeFi like yields without actually having to go at the full-blown DeFi.

520
00:38:07.560 --> 00:38:13.080
So people that stake BTC at the second stage, they will earn yield in Core.

521
00:38:13.420 --> 00:38:20.240
And then, you know, they will join the Core community automatically, kind of.

