571
00:42:01.940 --> 00:42:06.740
And I think we're past that because I think the market, A, no longer really rewards that.

572
00:42:07.180 --> 00:42:11.300
But B, there's not as much left, I think, in that tank, right?

573
00:42:11.340 --> 00:42:13.800
Like it's now about how do we actually scale things.

574
00:42:13.800 --> 00:42:26.320
And one of the things that Core prides itself on is being a product-focused blockchain versus research-focused blockchain, meaning that our goal is build stuff people want versus, you know, maybe write the newest, most novel, you know, theory.

575
00:42:26.680 --> 00:42:30.840
Which, not to say that there's not value in that, it's just most of that gets commoditized.

576
00:42:31.300 --> 00:42:33.780
And that commoditization is inevitable.

577
00:42:34.100 --> 00:42:36.400
And what ultimately comes back is the durable value.

578
00:42:36.580 --> 00:42:37.800
Do you actually have users?

579
00:42:37.920 --> 00:42:39.060
Do you actually have TVL?

580
00:42:39.160 --> 00:42:40.960
Do you have these two things intermixing?

581
00:42:41.220 --> 00:42:42.780
Are people using your protocols?

582
00:42:42.780 --> 00:42:48.520
And that's such a different viewpoint from many of these other chains.

583
00:42:48.600 --> 00:42:51.720
And I think long-term is such a differentiator for us.

584
00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:56.100
But to kind of go back to the root of the question, how do we get there?

585
00:42:56.160 --> 00:43:01.160
